name wx-ccrp-wind-1
timeout 200

# THE DELIVERY ERROR, AND WHAT IT IS MADE OF (re-measured after model delta D1 and the release round
# that followed it). Two errors used to hide inside one number; they are now separated and each is
# reported by the `stores DELIVERY` line:
#   predErrM  ~43 m  the FIRE CONTROL's own error: it integrates a stored table, the bomb flies the
#                    model's aerodynamics, and the difference is a declared property of every delivery
#                    (core/FBBallistics' banner). It is NOT corrected, and the ~45 m fragment radius
#                    is what it has to stay inside.
#   aimLongM  ~41 m  the delivered impact against the aim point. Its excess over predErrM is the
#                    RELEASE-MOMENT error, and after this round it is ~0: the pilot leads the cue by
#                    the bus latency PLUS his own decision tick, and he holds the run-in attitude until
#                    the SMS counter says the store has LEFT (before, he rolled into the escape turn
#                    during the actuation latency and released at 32 deg of bank: 64 m long, 11.5 m
#                    across).
# So the run ends SUCCESS again, and it does so because the release moment is right, not because two
# errors happen to cancel. If predErrM ever grows past 45 m this mission fails, and that is correct.

# THE SAME CCRP DELIVERY AS attack-ccrp.fbm, WITH A CROSSWIND — geometry, loadout, brief and target
# identical, one `wx` line added. It is the pair that is the measurement: run both and subtract.
#
# THE FIRE CONTROL DOES NOT KNOW ABOUT THE WIND, deliberately. modules/f16/FBF16FireControl integrates
# the store's stored ballistic table against a still-air fall (core/FBBallistics); nothing in FlightBox
# hands it a wind vector, because nothing in the real jet's ballistic solution would have one unless the
# pilot had entered it. So the bomb is released on a solution computed for air that is not there, is then
# carried downwind for its whole time of fall by the same FGWinds the aircraft flies in, and lands short
# of nothing and wide of the aimpoint by roughly
#
#   cross-track miss ~= crosswind * (time of fall - the seconds the round needs to relax into the airmass)
#
# THAT IS THE FINDING, not a defect: an uncorrected delivery in wind lands somewhere else, and by how
# much is a property of the weapon and the release height. `stores DELIVERY`'s aimAcrossM is the number;
# the calm run of attack-ccrp.fbm is the zero it is measured against (9.88 m -> 22.67 m, i.e. +12.8 m of
# cross-track error for 25 kt across).
#
# THE DRIFT IS SMALL, AND THAT IS ALSO A RESULT. "Wind times time of fall" would say 127 m; a 227 kg
# bomb doing 220 m/s couples to the air so weakly sideways that in ten seconds it barely notices — its
# lateral relaxation time is on the order of two minutes. So the target still dies here (exit 0, the
# bunker DESTROYED); at 100 kt across, the same mission leaves it standing. The mission exists to
# produce the number, not to fail.
#
# WIND FROM 360 at 25 kt: square across a run-in flown due east, so the entire wind is cross-track and
# almost none of it changes the release RANGE.

wx wind 360 25

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 6.80000  900 90.0 450       # due east at the target, co-track, 19 km out
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 46.90000 7.05000 900 450                # THE TARGET: the active steerpoint IS the aim point
  wp 46.95000 7.20000 3000 400               # the egress point, flown after the break turn
  objective kill unit bunker

unit bunker
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 46.90000 7.05000 ground 90.0 0
